  "title": "Job 3",
  "display_title": "Job 3",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 3,
  "sortOrder": 18003,
  "verseCount": 26,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "After this opened Job his mouth, and cursed his day.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And Job spake, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Let the day perish wherein I was born, and the night in which it was said, There is a man child conceived.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Let that day be darkness; let not God regard it from above, neither let the light shine upon it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Let darkness and the shadow of death stain it; let a cloud dwell upon it; let the blackness of the day terrify it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "As for that night, let darkness seize upon it; let it not be joined unto the days of the year, let it not come into the number of the months.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Lo, let that night be solitary, let no joyful voice come therein.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Let them curse it that curse the day, who are ready to raise up their mourning.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Let the stars of the twilight thereof be dark; let it look for light, but have none; neither let it see the dawning of the day:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Because it shut not up the doors of my mother’s womb, nor hid sorrow from mine eyes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Why died I not from the womb? why did I not give up the ghost when I came out of the belly?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Why did the knees prevent me? or why the breasts that I should suck?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "For now should I have lain still and been quiet, I should have slept: then had I been at rest,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "With kings and counsellors of the earth, which built desolate places for themselves;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Or with princes that had gold, who filled their houses with silver:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Or as an hidden untimely birth I had not been; as infants which never saw light.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "There the wicked cease from troubling; and there the weary be at rest.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "There the prisoners rest together; they hear not the voice of the oppressor.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "The small and great are there; and the servant is free from his master.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Wherefore is light given to him that is in misery, and life unto the bitter in soul;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Which long for death, but it cometh not; and dig for it more than for hid treasures;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Which rejoice exceedingly, and are glad, when they can find the grave?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Why is light given to a man whose way is hid, and whom God hath hedged in?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "For my sighing cometh before I eat, and my roarings are poured out like the waters.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "For the thing which I greatly feared is come upon me, and that which I was afraid of is come unto me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:3:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "I was not in safety, neither had I rest, neither was I quiet; yet trouble came.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 3:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:3:26"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
